1
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:06,850
{\an8}This is Layout. It shows how the cards are arranged on your dash.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,450
{\an8}Drag a card to move it wherever you want.

3
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:19,050
{\an8}Drag a handle to resize it.

4
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:25,850
{\an8}Very small cards can't show every widget. Experiment, and check the preview.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:30,325
{\an8}While you drag, cards snap to the best size and position.

6
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:36,225
{\an8}Every change can be undone.

7
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:39,975
{\an8}Discard takes you back to the last version you saved.

8
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:47,025
{\an8}So: the dock on one side, then columns of cards you can resize.

9
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:53,475
{\an8}Click plus at the side to add a column, while the screen has room for it.

10
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,600
{\an8}At some point the screen is full, and no more columns fit.

11
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:04,250
{\an8}To remove a card or column, click its minus button.

12
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:09,250
{\an8}New columns can go on the left or on the right.

13
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,250
{\an8}Or click New column at the bottom.

14
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,625
{\an8}It stops adding columns once the screen is full.

15
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:24,450
{\an8}Add card adds a single card.

16
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:29,725
{\an8}Every card holds one widget, like an OBD value or live ride data.

17
00:01:30,275 --> 00:01:34,725
{\an8}The fuel value is estimated from the settings you entered on the phone.

18
00:01:36,925 --> 00:01:40,900
{\an8}Next, in the Widgets video, you'll choose what each card shows.
